[Music]  so i just moved into my apartment and i  really wanted to do something cool with  the kitchen i love arcade games so i  turned my kitchen from this  to this  so first i started off with the grass  wall it's basically a bunch of 20 by 20  grass squares from amazon that you  connect into lines to fit your wall  you can also add or subtract them in  halves as well to attach them to the  wall all you need is a staple gun and  staples that being said this project is  not for everybody there are other  options that you can hang the grass  balls up with but i personally did not  like them and i didn't think they worked  for my specific wall but feel free to  try them so overall i want to say the  grass while it took me anywhere from an  hour and a half to two hours to put up  luckily i had my big cousin visiting  from new orleans to help me out because  it's definitely a two-person project  alright so next up was the neon sign so  basically all i did was loop a string  that was provided to me through the neon  sign put a nail on the wall and hung it  up all right so now for the fun part the  rk machines arcade one up sent me a few  arcade machines and set them up was  super easy it takes about 30 to 45  minutes per machine but all you need is  a screwdriver and they provide  everything else you need honestly i have  so many memories from playing arcades  when i was younger from my mom always  taking me to the dollar movie theater  and anytime we went we would go an hour  early so we could play a couple arcade  games her favorite game was miss pac-man  so obviously that became my favorite i  love miss pac-man me and her have  competitions all the time we're so  competitive at it and we just love that  game so much  another memory is from my dad taking me  and my brothers bowling all the time we  were a bowling family and one game they  always had at the bowling alley was big  buck hunting and that became my second  favorite game i love to play it and i  don't think anybody can beat me if i  play i'm gonna win that's how i feel  about it okay i'ma just throw it out  there  if you notice every arcade game comes  with a really cool bass we have pac-man  big buck hunter pro x-man vs street  fighter and miss pac-man and each game  has at least four or five other games on  it after that i had to fix the neon  light a little bit just to fit the  aesthetic that i wanted added my two of  ms pac-man 40th anniversary stools so to  fit the vibe that i wanted from my  kitchen i got this really cool bar type  of counter slash kitchen table from  wayfair and i think it just fit the vibe  perfectly i'm here by myself so i don't  need a huge kitchen table  so i'm excited to have this set up i  feel good that now when i invite my  friends over i have a spot that we can  just hang out and not have to go out to  the crowded bars we can just hang at my  house kick it play some games have a  couple drinks  [Music]  if you do try this drop some pictures in  the comments and i would love to see how  you either built your grass wall or  transform your house into one of your  childhood dreams  [Music]  you

